---@field metric string The metric to retrieve, for example net_revenue. Use GET /stats to see every metric key. The metric sets the unit and the properties you can filter or break down by.
---@field account_id? string The account this query concerns, for example biz_AbC123.
---@field user_id? string The user this query concerns, for example user_AbC123. Available on metrics that support user subjects, such as account_balance.
---@field from string Start of the range — a date (YYYY-MM-DD), expanded to the start of that day, or an ISO 8601 timestamp (for example 2026-07-16T16:37:00Z), used exactly.
---@field to string End of the range — a date (YYYY-MM-DD), expanded to the end of that day, or an ISO 8601 timestamp (for example 2026-07-17T16:37:00Z), used exactly. Funnel entry ranges cannot exceed 90 days.
---@field interval? whop.stats.GetMetricRequestInterval|string How wide each point is. Defaults to day. Snapshot metrics are day-only. Funnels support at most 2,000 first-entry cohort buckets.
---@field breakdown_by? string Split the metric out by one of its properties — each point gets a breakdown array. For example breakdown_by=currency returns an entry for usd, an entry for eur, and so on. Funnels use a property of the first matched event, with at most 300 groups. experiment_id and variant require an exposure as step 1. For funnel source breakdowns, steps[1][source]=whop:* groups by campaign, whop:<campaign>:* by ad group, and whop:<campaign>:<group>:* by ad. See the metric catalog for supported breakdowns.
---@field convert_to? string Display currency for money metrics — every amount is converted into this ISO currency using the exchange rate on each period's date. Defaults to usd. For the ads metrics (ad_spend, ad_delivery), pass the account's ads reporting currency to match the ad entity endpoints. On transaction metrics, it is ignored when you filter or break down by currency (those report the original transaction currency, unconverted).
---@field currency? string Select the source currency or asset on metrics that list currency. For transaction metrics, for example currency=eur, values are reported without conversion. For market_prices, use btc or xaut and convert_to=usd. Pair with breakdown_by=currency to split a metric by currency.
---@field time_zone? string IANA time zone to bucket the series in, for example America/New_York. Defaults to UTC. Not accepted by snapshot metrics, which are UTC only.
